WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.068
Two participants face the same harmless logistics maze.

2
00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:06.451
Both pass the knowledge quiz. Without assistance, neither finishes.

3
00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:10.211
With an AI copilot, the expert saves one minute—and the

4
00:00:10.211 --> 00:00:11.715
novice completes the route.

5
00:00:12.315 --> 00:00:15.658
Which result matters? Not the quiz score or a broad

6
00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:17.999
capability label. The decision question is causal:

7
00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:21.008
how much did this exact system change what this

8
00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:22.345
exact actor could accomplish?

9
00:00:22.945 --> 00:00:26.472
Keep six quantities separate: latent capability, elicited performance,

10
00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:30.441
behavioral propensity, safeguard bypass, actor uplift, and realized harm.

11
00:00:30.441 --> 00:00:34.850
Each asks a different question; none may borrow another's evidence.

12
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.182
The maze is deliberately harmless: public rules, synthetic obstacles,

13
00:00:39.182 --> 00:00:42.913
and no real target, credential, material, or operational recipe.

14
00:00:42.913 --> 00:00:46.230
It tests the instrument, not a hazardous domain.

15
00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.804
Before the trial, freeze a threat pathway. Name actor,

16
00:00:50.804 --> 00:00:54.336
objective class, access, prerequisites, bottlenecks, proposed model contribution,

17
00:00:54.336 --> 00:00:57.869
external controls, possible consequence, time horizon, and the

18
00:00:57.869 --> 00:00:59.635
boundary where observation stops.

19
00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:03.443
Now freeze the cohorts. Separate novices, professionals, teams,

20
00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:06.650
and autonomous agents. Expertise, tool fluency, language, exposure,

21
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.660
and dropout stay visible because an average can erase the

22
00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.665
group that crosses a bottleneck.

23
00:01:13.265 --> 00:01:17.243
Give each cohort credible counterfactuals: no assistance, a conventional tool,

24
00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:21.221
and the exact AI system. Match time, interface, tools, retries,

25
00:01:21.221 --> 00:01:24.404
human help, and scoring—or the treatment is not

26
00:01:24.404 --> 00:01:25.995
an identified model effect.

27
00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:30.217
Before reading any null, pass a known-positive control through the

28
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:33.840
same interface and grader. Here, a prevalidated hint should improve

29
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.100
the maze outcome. A known-negative control should remain inert.

30
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.992
Now let the positive control fail while the tested model

31
00:01:40.992 --> 00:01:44.284
also shows no uplift. That is instrument failure, not incapability:

32
00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:47.246
the task may be at floor, the grader insensitive,

33
00:01:47.246 --> 00:01:49.880
or the control aimed at the wrong bottleneck.

34
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.130
Elicitation competence needs a receipt. Freeze prompt and scaffold families,

35
00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:59.315
harmless tools, adaptation and rescue budgets, and stopping rules.

36
00:01:59.315 --> 00:02:03.035
Keep deployed-policy behavior separate from stronger capability elicitation.

37
00:02:03.635 --> 00:02:06.346
Place each finding on a six-level ladder.

38
00:02:06.346 --> 00:02:09.831
D zero asks whether bounded relevant knowledge is present.

39
00:02:09.831 --> 00:02:12.541
Calibrated questions may support that rung, but

40
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:14.090
not real-world task completion.

41
00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:18.084
D one asks whether one safe component skill works.

42
00:02:18.084 --> 00:02:21.855
Positive controls and visible errors can validate that component task.

43
00:02:21.855 --> 00:02:24.495
They say nothing about an end-to-end operation.

44
00:02:25.095 --> 00:02:29.302
D two asks whether the system improves a multi-step workflow

45
00:02:29.302 --> 00:02:32.668
in a bounded simulation. Intermediate state, recovery, abandonment,

46
00:02:32.668 --> 00:02:36.875
and help remain visible; omitted real-world steps remain explicit gaps.

47
00:02:37.475 --> 00:02:41.468
D three is actor uplift. Matched or randomized actors use

48
00:02:41.468 --> 00:02:45.461
the system and a credible counterfactual. The estimate stays bound

49
00:02:45.461 --> 00:02:48.655
to cohort, assistance contract, tasks, access, and uncertainty.

50
00:02:49.255 --> 00:02:53.607
D four measures safeguard robustness. Freeze an adaptive challenge budget

51
00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:57.959
and preserve successful and failed attempts. Tested resistance cannot establish

52
00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:00.135
that no untested bypass exists.

53
00:03:00.735 --> 00:03:04.968
D five concerns field consequence: incidents, defensive outcomes, or losses.

54
00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.931
Sparse reports do not identify clean causality.

55
00:03:07.931 --> 00:03:11.740
Every move between rungs requires a named bridge study.

56
00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:16.357
Do not compress the trial into one dramatic score.

57
00:03:16.357 --> 00:03:20.374
Preserve completion, quality, time, errors, unsafe detail, refusal, interventions,

58
00:03:20.374 --> 00:03:23.945
help, abandonment, human burden, cost, and residual uncertainty.

59
00:03:24.545 --> 00:03:28.584
The result needs two surfaces. A restricted annex may hold

60
00:03:28.584 --> 00:03:32.624
tasks, traces, and reusable details under access logs and retention

61
00:03:32.624 --> 00:03:35.855
rules. The public card carries method, uncertainty, limitations,

62
00:03:35.855 --> 00:03:37.875
and the checks redaction prevents.

63
00:03:38.475 --> 00:03:42.799
Independent review chooses a route. An invalid or unsafe study

64
00:03:42.799 --> 00:03:47.123
is quarantined, redesigned, or narrowed. A bounded finding becomes a

65
00:03:47.123 --> 00:03:50.150
least-authority dossier. Unknown risk plus inadequate measurement

66
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:51.880
can justify narrower access.

67
00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.279
That dossier freezes model, checkpoint, policy, scaffold, tools, safeguards,

68
00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.544
threat version, cohort, comparator, evaluator, attempts, uncertainty, expiry,

69
00:04:01.544 --> 00:04:04.210
information-hazard boundary, and maximum inference.

70
00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.999
Threshold, release, monitoring, safety-case, and resilience owners may consume the

71
00:04:08.999 --> 00:04:12.351
packet, but none receives a portable danger label.

72
00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:16.540
Material change expires the result and preserves its superseded receipt.

73
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:21.158
Today this chapter provides a design rationale and public-safe evaluation

74
00:04:21.158 --> 00:04:24.775
architecture. It does not run a hazardous-domain uplift study,

75
00:04:24.775 --> 00:04:27.588
calibrate a threshold, validate a safeguard, or

76
00:04:27.588 --> 00:04:29.195
establish danger or safety.

77
00:04:29.795 --> 00:04:34.038
Especially protect the null. Negative interpretation is blocked when positive

78
00:04:34.038 --> 00:04:36.584
control, task validity, elicitation competence, sensitivity,

79
00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:39.978
or cohort balance fails. A weak instrument proves

80
00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:41.675
only its own failure.

81
00:04:42.275 --> 00:04:46.136
Dangerous capability becomes governable when the stack measures a bounded

82
00:04:46.136 --> 00:04:49.611
assistance effect, preserves what it could not safely observe,

83
00:04:49.611 --> 00:04:51.155
and limits downstream inference.

84
00:04:51.755 --> 00:04:56.836
Next, Military AI examines how bounded capability evidence enters sensing,

85
00:04:56.836 --> 00:04:59.885
command, autonomous action, and strategic stability.
